# VTID-03929 — commands run during this change

## Investigation
Read services/gateway/src/services/aws-ecs-readonly.ts's own header comment
in full before touching anything: OPERATOR_AWS_READONLY_ENABLED ships
default-off deliberately, because this client runs under the gateway's
existing broad IAM role rather than a dedicated narrow one.

## Attempted narrow-role approach (abandoned on explicit owner instruction)
$ cd services/gateway && npm install @aws-sdk/credential-providers@^3.1094.0 --save
(added 2 packages)
Interrupted by the platform owner: "Who told you to build a narrow AWS
role? I want a broad AWS role... No way to do a narrow role. It must have
the maximum broad one."

$ npm uninstall @aws-sdk/credential-providers
$ git status --short package.json package-lock.json
(clean — no diff, dependency fully reverted)

## Fix
Rewrote aws-ecs-readonly.ts's header comment to record the explicit
decision. Added OPERATOR_AWS_READONLY_ENABLED=true to
.github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml's task-def jq block
(strip list + set list), same pattern as its two already-enabled
siblings OPERATOR_CODEBASE_READ_ENABLED / OPERATOR_DB_READONLY_ENABLED.

## AWS IAM permission check (informational — this session's own creds)
$ aws iam get-user
AccessDenied — explicit deny in permissions boundary
arn:aws:iam::472838866351:policy/claude-code-aws-agent-boundary
(This session's own IAM user cannot create/inspect IAM roles or policies
at all — confirmed this is a hard AWS-side deny, not a judgment call.
Irrelevant to the final approach since no new role is being created —
recorded here only because it was checked before the owner's broad-role
instruction made it moot.)

